      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors That Change the Price"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size and Pitch: Steeper slopes (like a 7/12 or 10/12 pitch) increase labor difficulty and safety equipment needs.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Materials: Standard asphalt shingles are the most affordable, while metal, tile, or impact-resistant shingles designed for Utah\u2019s heavy snow and high-altitude UV/hailstorms cost significantly more.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-Off and Sheeting: Removing multiple old layers of shingles or replacing rotted plywood/decking adds to the labor and disposal fees.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
